      "morphological_conclusion": "All 9 W3-detected stars within 60 arcsec (7 within 41.5 arcsec) lie along a NE-SW Galactic cirrus ridge and exhibit systematically elevated AllWISE W3 PSF reduced chi-square (chi2W3 = 1.069 to 1.701, mean 1.299, peaking at chi2W3 = 1.701 on KIC 6634976) compared to off-ridge upper-limit stars (mean chi2W3 = 0.957). This confirms that extended diffuse 12um PAH / 22um dust emission (SFD E(B-V) = 0.3338 mag, 100um brightness = 21.32 MJy/sr) contaminates the 6.5\" W3 and 12.0\" W4 apertures in list-driven AllWISE photometry forced at W1/W2 positions."
